{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_96","type":"command_execution","command":"\"D:\\\\software\\\\PowerShell\\\\pwsh-7.6.6\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'cat tests/unit/deep/a1-deep.test.ts; echo \"=====A2=====\"; cat tests/unit/deep/a2-deep.test.ts; echo \"=====A3=====\"; cat tests/unit/deep/a3-deep.test.ts'","aggregated_output":"import { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\r\n\r\nimport {\r\n  type WriteRiskProfile,\r\n  DEFAULT_WRITE_RISK_PROFILE,\r\n  MissingWriteRiskProfileError,\r\n  assertWriteRiskProfileForTool,\r\n  requiresApproval,\r\n  requiresFullFsDiff,\r\n  validateWriteRiskProfile,\r\n} from '../../../openclaw_runtime/src/shared/tool-registration.js';\r\nimport {\r\n  beginSnapshot,\r\n  collectDeclaredWritePaths,\r\n} from '../../../openclaw_runtime/src/agents/sessions/extensions/policy-light-snapshotter.js';\r\nimport {\r\n  ShadowWriteEventRecorder,\r\n  detectUndeclaredWrites,\r\n} from '../../../openclaw_runtime/src/agents/sessions/extensions/shadow-write-event-recorder.js';\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * A1 deep tests — Layered Execution Isolation.\r\n *\r\n * Covers three source modules:\r\n * - shared/tool-registration.ts (WriteRiskProfile enforcement)\r\n * - sessions/extensions/policy-light-snapshotter.ts (declared-path collection + snapshot)\r\n * - sessions/extensions/shadow-write-event-recorder.ts (undeclared-write detection)\r\n *\r\n * Note on import depth: tests live in tests/unit/deep/, so the relative path to\r\n * the runtime tree is ../../../openclaw_runtime/src/... (three levels up to root).\r\n */\r\n\r\ndescribe('A1 deep — tool-registration / policy-light-snapshotter / shadow-write-event-recorder', () => {\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  // 1. 功能完整性 (4 tests)\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  describe('功能完整性', () => {\r\n    it('requiresFullFsDiff returns false for no_writes / declared_paths / pattern_writes', () => {\r\n      expect(requiresFullFsDiff({ kind: 'no_writes' })).toBe(false);\r\n      expect(requiresFullFsDiff({ kind: 'declared_paths', writePaths: ['a.txt'] })).toBe(false);\r\n      expect(requiresFullFsDiff({ kind: 'pattern_writes', writePattern: '*.log' })).toBe(false);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('requiresFullFsDiff returns true only for dynamic_writes', () => {\r\n      expect(requiresFullFsDiff({ kind: 'dynamic_writes', requiresApproval: true })).toBe(true);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('requiresApproval returns false for no_writes / declared_paths / pattern_writes', () => {\r\n      expect(requiresApproval({ kind: 'no_writes' })).toBe(false);\r\n      expect(requiresApproval({ kind: 'declared_paths', writePaths: ['a.txt'] })).toBe(false);\r\n      expect(requiresApproval({ kind: 'pattern_writes', writePattern: '*.log' })).toBe(false);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('requiresApproval returns true for dynamic_writes and DEFAULT_WRITE_RISK_PROFILE', () => {\r\n      expect(requiresApproval({ kind: 'dynamic_writes', requiresApproval: true })).toBe(true);\r\n      expect(requiresApproval(DEFAULT_WRITE_RISK_PROFILE)).toBe(true);\r\n      expect(DEFAULT_WRITE_RISK_PROFILE.kind).toBe('dynamic_writes');\r\n    });\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  // 2. 边界条件 (5 tests)\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  describe('边界条件', () => {\r\n    it('declared_paths with an empty writePaths array fails validation', () => {\r\n      const error = validateWriteRiskProfile({ kind: 'declared_paths', writePaths: [] });\r\n      expect(error).not.toBeNull();\r\n      expect(error).toContain('writePaths');\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('declared_paths without a writePaths field fails validation', () => {\r\n      expect(validateWriteRiskProfile({ kind: 'declared_paths' })).not.toBeNull();\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('pattern_writes without a writePattern (or empty) fails validation', () => {\r\n      expect(validateWriteRiskProfile({ kind: 'pattern_writes' })).not.toBeNull();\r\n      expect(validateWriteRiskProfile({ kind: 'pattern_writes', writePattern: '' })).toContain(\r\n        'writePattern',\r\n      );\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('collectDeclaredWritePaths with empty input returns empty declared paths and dynamic tools', () => {\r\n      const result = collectDeclaredWritePaths([]);\r\n      expect(result.declaredPaths).toEqual([]);\r\n      expect(result.dynamicTools).toEqual([]);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('collectDeclaredWritePaths with mixed kinds separates declared paths from dynamic tools', () => {\r\n      const result = collectDeclaredWritePaths([\r\n        { name: 'readonly', profile: { kind: 'no_writes' } },\r\n        { name: 'writer', profile: { kind: 'declared_paths', writePaths: ['a.txt', 'b.txt'] } },\r\n        { name: 'patterner', profile: { kind: 'pattern_writes', writePattern: '*.log' } },\r\n        { name: 'dynamic', profile: { kind: 'dynamic_writes', requiresApproval: true } },\r\n      ]);\r\n      // Patterns are folded into declaredPaths (git-diff interprets them); no_writes contributes nothing.\r\n      expect(result.declaredPaths).toEqual(['a.txt', 'b.txt', '*.log']);\r\n      expect(result.dynamicTools).toEqual(['dynamic']);\r\n    });\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  // 3. 错误路径 (5 tests)\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  describe('错误路径', () => {\r\n    it('assertWriteRiskProfileForTool does not throw for readonly + undefined profile', () => {\r\n      expect(() => assertWriteRiskProfileForTool('readonly', undefined)).not.toThrow();\r\n      expect(() => assertWriteRiskProfileForTool('readonly', { kind: 'no_writes' })).not.toThrow();\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('assertWriteRiskProfileForTool throws MissingWriteRiskProfileError (field=\"writeRiskProfile\") for write + undefined', () => {\r\n      try {\r\n        assertWriteRiskProfileForTool('write', undefined);\r\n        throw new Error('expected assertWriteRiskProfileForTool to throw');\r\n      } catch (err) {\r\n        expect(err).toBeInstanceOf(MissingWriteRiskProfileError);\r\n        expect((err as MissingWriteRiskProfileError).field).toBe('writeRiskProfile');\r\n      }\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('assertWriteRiskProfileForTool throws for destructive + declared_paths (destructive requires dynamic_writes)', () => {\r\n      expect(() =>\r\n        assertWriteRiskProfileForTool('destructive', {\r\n          kind: 'declared_paths',\r\n          writePaths: ['a.txt'],\r\n        }),\r\n      ).toThrow(MissingWriteRiskProfileError);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('validateWriteRiskProfile returns the required-message for null input', () => {\r\n      expect(validateWriteRiskProfile(null)).toBe(\r\n        'writeRiskProfile is required for write-capable tools',\r\n      );\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('validateWriteRiskProfile returns errors for non-object input and missing-kind input', () => {\r\n      expect(validateWriteRiskProfile('not-an-object')).toBe(\r\n        'writeRiskProfile is required for write-capable tools',\r\n      );\r\n      expect(validateWriteRiskProfile({})).toMatch(/kind must be one of/);\r\n    });\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  // 4. 属性测试 (3 tests)\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  describe('属性测试', () => {\r\n    it('dynamic_writes tools never produce undeclared write events (recorder short-circuits)', () => {\r\n      // The dynamic_writes short-circuit lives in ShadowWriteEventRecorder, not the\r\n      // pure detectUndeclaredWrites (which has no profile notion and only compares paths).\r\n      const recorder = new ShadowWriteEventRecorder([\r\n        { name: 'dyn', profile: { kind: 'dynamic_writes', requiresApproval: true } },\r\n      ]);\r\n      recorder.recordActualWrites('dyn', [\r\n        'anywhere/file.txt',\r\n        'another/path.ts',\r\n        'x/y/z.json',\r\n      ]);\r\n      expect(recorder.getEvents()).toEqual([]);\r\n      expect(recorder.hasEvents()).toBe(false);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('no_writes scenario flags every actual write as undeclared (pure detectUndeclaredWrites with empty declared set)', () => {\r\n      const result = detectUndeclaredWrites([], ['a.txt', 'dir/b.txt']);\r\n      expect(result.hasUndeclared).toBe(true);\r\n      expect(result.undeclaredPaths).toEqual(['a.txt', 'dir/b.txt']);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('detectUndeclaredWrites normalizes backslashes to forward slashes and matches case-insensitively', () => {\r\n      // Declared 'Output/File.txt' should cover 'output\\file.txt' and 'OUTPUT\\FILE.TXT'\r\n      // (normalizePath: backslash -> forward slash, lowercase).\r\n      const result = detectUndeclaredWrites(\r\n        ['Output/File.txt'],\r\n        ['output\\\\file.txt', 'OUTPUT\\\\FILE.TXT'],\r\n      );\r\n      expect(result.undeclaredPaths).toEqual([]);\r\n      expect(result.hasUndeclared).toBe(false);\r\n    });\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  // 5. 并发测试 (3 tests)\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  describe('并发测试', () => {\r\n    it('interleaved recordActualWrites calls for different tools do not interfere', () => {\r\n      const recorder = new ShadowWriteEventRecorder([\r\n        { name: 'w1', profile: { kind: 'declared_paths', writePaths: ['only-w1.txt'] } },\r\n        { name: 'w2', profile: { kind: 'declared_paths', writePaths: ['only-w2.txt'] } },\r\n      ]);\r\n      // Two \"workers\" recording writes in interleaved order.\r\n      recorder.recordActualWrites('w1', ['only-w1.txt', 'leak-to-w2.txt']);\r\n      recorder.recordActualWrites('w2', ['only-w2.txt', 'leak-to-w1.txt']);\r\n      const events = recorder.getEvents();\r\n      const w1Paths = events.filter((e) => e.toolName === 'w1').map((e) => e.path);\r\n      const w2Paths = events.filter((e) => e.toolName === 'w2').map((e) => e.path);\r\n      expect(w1Paths).toEqual(['leak-to-w2.txt']);\r\n      expect(w2Paths).toEqual(['leak-to-w1.txt']);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('clear() empties recorded events', () => {\r\n      const recorder = new ShadowWriteEventRecorder([\r\n        { name: 'nw', profile: { kind: 'no_writes' } },\r\n      ]);\r\n      recorder.recordActualWrites('nw', ['a.txt']);\r\n      expect(recorder.hasEvents()).toBe(true);\r\n      recorder.clear();\r\n      expect(recorder.getEvents()).toEqual([]);\r\n      expect(recorder.hasEvents()).toBe(false);\r\n      expect(recorder.getEventCount()).toBe(0);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('getEventCount and hasEvents stay consistent across mutations', () => {\r\n      const recorder = new ShadowWriteEventRecorder([\r\n        { name: 'nw', profile: { kind: 'no_writes' } },\r\n      ]);\r\n      expect(recorder.getEventCount()).toBe(0);\r\n      expect(recorder.hasEvents()).toBe(false);\r\n      recorder.recordActualWrites('nw', ['a', 'b', 'c']);\r\n      expect(recorder.getEventCount()).toBe(3);\r\n      expect(recorder.hasEvents()).toBe(true);\r\n    });\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  // 6. 压力测试 (2 tests)\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  describe('压力测试', () => {\r\n    it('collectDeclaredWritePaths handles 1000 declared paths under 50ms', () => {\r\n      const tools = Array.from({ length: 1000 }, (_, i) => ({\r\n        name: `tool-${i}`,\r\n        profile: {\r\n          kind: 'declared_paths' as const,\r\n          writePaths: [`path-${i}.txt`],\r\n        },\r\n      }));\r\n      const start = Date.now();\r\n      const result = collectDeclaredWritePaths(tools);\r\n      const elapsed = Date.now() - start;\r\n      expect(result.declaredPaths.length).toBe(1000);\r\n      expect(elapsed).toBeLessThan(50);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('ShadowWriteEventRecorder processes 10000 actual writes without crashing', () => {\r\n      const recorder = new ShadowWriteEventRecorder([\r\n        { name: 'nw', profile: { kind: 'no_writes' } },\r\n      ]);\r\n      const paths = Array.from({ length: 10000 }, (_, i) => `file-${i}.txt`);\r\n      expect(() => recorder.recordActualWrites('nw', paths)).not.toThrow();\r\n      expect(recorder.getEventCount()).toBe(10000);\r\n    });\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  // 7. 集成测试 (2 tests)\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  describe('集成测试', () => {\r\n    it('assertWriteRiskProfileForTool simulates a realistic tool registration flow (and beginSnapshot flag-off parity)', async () => {\r\n      // readonly tool without a profile -> pass.\r\n      expect(() => assertWriteRiskProfileForTool('readonly', undefined)).not.toThrow();\r\n      // write tool with dynamic_writes -> pass.\r\n      expect(() =>\r\n        assertWriteRiskProfileForTool('write', {\r\n          kind: 'dynamic_writes',\r\n          requiresApproval: true,\r\n        } satisfies WriteRiskProfile),\r\n      ).not.toThrow();\r\n      // destructive tool with dynamic_writes -> pass.\r\n      expect(() =>\r\n        assertWriteRiskProfileForTool('destructive', {\r\n          kind: 'dynamic_writes',\r\n          requiresApproval: true,\r\n        } satisfies WriteRiskProfile),\r\n      ).not.toThrow();\r\n      // S2 fix (P0): write tool with no_writes profile is now REJECTED\r\n      // (semantic incompatibility — write-capable tool cannot declare no_writes).\r\n      expect(() => assertWriteRiskProfileForTool('write', { kind: 'no_writes' })).toThrow(\r\n        MissingWriteRiskProfileError,\r\n      );\r\n\r\n      // beginSnapshot flag-off parity: with a1 disabled it returns a no-op handle\r\n      // without touching the filesystem or git (covers beginSnapshot / SnapshotHandle / SnapshotPlan).\r\n      const snap = await beginSnapshot([], { workspaceRoot: '.', a1Enabled: false });\r\n      expect(snap.ok).toBe(true);\r\n      if (snap.ok) {\r\n        expect(typeof snap.handle.commit).toBe('function');\r\n        expect(snap.handle.plan.mode).toBe('copy-on-write');\r\n        expect(snap.handle.plan.declaredWritePaths).toEqual([]);\r\n      }\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('MissingWriteRiskProfileError is an Error subclass and carries field=\"writeRiskProfile\"', () => {\r\n      const err = new MissingWriteRiskProfileError('boom');\r\n      expect(err).toBeInstanceOf(Error);\r\n      expect(err.field).toBe('writeRiskProfile');\r\n      expect(err.name).toBe('MissingWriteRiskProfileError');\r\n\r\n      // A thrown instance preserves the prototype chain.\r\n      try {\r\n        assertWriteRiskProfileForTool('write', undefined);\r\n        throw new Error('expected throw');\r\n      } catch (e) {\r\n        expect(e).toBeInstanceOf(Error);\r\n        expect(e).toBeInstanceOf(MissingWriteRiskProfileError);\r\n      }\r\n    });\r\n  });\r\n});\r\n=====A2=====\r\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\r\n\r\nimport {\r\n  buildExecutionWaves,\r\n  buildTaskGraph,\r\n  type OrchestrationTaskGraph,\r\n  type OrchestrationTaskNode,\r\n} from '../../../openclaw_runtime/src/agents/orchestration-protocol.js';\r\nimport {\r\n  type WavePlan,\r\n  ResourceAwareWaveScheduler,\r\n} from '../../../openclaw_runtime/src/agents/resource-aware-wave-scheduler.js';\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * A2 deep tests — Resource-aware wave scheduling + orchestration protocol.\r\n *\r\n * Covers:\r\n * - agents/resource-aware-wave-scheduler.ts (ResourceAwareWaveScheduler, WavePlan, WaveStatus, RePlanRequest, RePlanResult)\r\n * - agents/orchestration-protocol.ts (buildExecutionWaves, buildTaskGraph, OrchestrationTaskGraph, OrchestrationExecutionWave)\r\n *\r\n * Note on import depth: tests live in tests/unit/deep/, so the relative path to\r\n * the runtime tree is ../../../openclaw_runtime/src/... (three levels up to root).\r\n */\r\n\r\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n// Helpers\r\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\nfunction makeNode(\r\n  id: string,\r\n  deps: string[] = [],\r\n  role = 'worker',\r\n): OrchestrationTaskNode {\r\n  return {\r\n    taskNodeId: id,\r\n    roleName: role,\r\n    task: `Task ${id}`,\r\n    phase: 'worker',\r\n    dependsOn: deps,\r\n    scope: 'default',\r\n    requiredCapabilities: [],\r\n    attemptPolicy: { maxRepairAttempts: 0, maxRedoAttempts: 0 },\r\n    status: 'planned',\r\n  };\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction makeGraph(\r\n  nodeCount: number,\r\n  depsFn?: (index: number, id: string) => string[],\r\n): OrchestrationTaskGraph {\r\n  const nodes: OrchestrationTaskNode[] = Array.from({ length: nodeCount }, (_, i) => {\r\n    const id = `task-${i + 1}`;\r\n    return makeNode(id, depsFn ? depsFn(i, id) : []);\r\n  });\r\n  return { graphRunId: 'run-1', mode: 'router' as never, status: 'planned', nodes, edges: [] };\r\n}\r\n\r\ndescribe('A2 deep — orchestration-protocol / resource-aware-wave-scheduler', () => {\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  // 1. 功能完整性 (8 tests)\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  describe('功能完整性', () => {\r\n    it('buildExecutionWaves: 3 tasks / 2 workers -> 2 waves', () => {\r\n      const waves = buildExecutionWaves(makeGraph(3), 2);\r\n      expect(waves.length).toBe(2);\r\n      expect(waves[0].wave).toBe(1);\r\n      expect(waves[1].wave).toBe(2);\r\n      expect(waves[0].taskNodeIds).toEqual(['task-1', 'task-2']);\r\n      expect(waves[1].taskNodeIds).toEqual(['task-3']);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('buildExecutionWaves: graph with a verifier node places the verifier last', () => {\r\n      const graph = buildTaskGraph({\r\n        graphRunId: 'run-v',\r\n        mode: 'router' as never,\r\n        workers: [\r\n          { roleName: 'implementer', task: 'do work' },\r\n          { roleName: 'implementer', task: 'do more' },\r\n        ],\r\n        verifierRole: 'reviewer',\r\n        verifierTask: 'verify all',\r\n        requiredCapabilities: [],\r\n      });\r\n      const waves = buildExecutionWaves(graph, 10);\r\n      expect(waves.length).toBe(2);\r\n      // Verifier depends on both workers -> cannot be in wave 1.\r\n      expect(waves[0].taskNodeIds).toEqual(expect.arrayContaining(['implementer-1', 'implementer-2']));\r\n      expect(waves[0].taskNodeIds).not.toContain('reviewer-1');\r\n      expect(waves[1].taskNodeIds).toEqual(['reviewer-1']);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('wave.taskNodeIds concatenate to the full node set without duplicates', () => {\r\n      const waves = buildExecutionWaves(makeGraph(5), 2);\r\n      const allIds = waves.flatMap((w) => w.taskNodeIds);\r\n      expect(allIds).toEqual(['task-1', 'task-2', 'task-3', 'task-4', 'task-5']);\r\n      expect(new Set(allIds).size).toBe(5);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('wave.roles are unique within a wave when nodes have distinct roles', () => {\r\n      const graph: OrchestrationTaskGraph = {\r\n        graphRunId: 'run-r',\r\n        mode: 'router' as never,\r\n        status: 'planned',\r\n        nodes: [\r\n          makeNode('t1', [], 'implementer'),\r\n          makeNode('t2', [], 'architect'),\r\n          makeNode('t3', [], 'tester'),\r\n        ],\r\n        edges: [],\r\n      };\r\n      const waves = buildExecutionWaves(graph, 10);\r\n      expect(waves.length).toBe(1);\r\n      expect(new Set(waves[0].roles).size).toBe(waves[0].roles.length);\r\n      expect(waves[0].roles).toEqual(['implementer', 'architect', 'tester']);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('buildExecutionWaves on an empty graph returns an empty array', () => {\r\n      const empty: OrchestrationTaskGraph = {\r\n        graphRunId: 'run-e',\r\n        mode: 'router' as never,\r\n        status: 'planned',\r\n        nodes: [],\r\n        edges: [],\r\n      };\r\n      expect(buildExecutionWaves(empty)).toEqual([]);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('a single-node graph produces exactly one wave', () => {\r\n      const waves = buildExecutionWaves(makeGraph(1));\r\n      expect(waves.length).toBe(1);\r\n      expect(waves[0].taskNodeIds).toEqual(['task-1']);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('maxWorkers > tasks collapses all tasks into a single wave', () => {\r\n      const waves = buildExecutionWaves(makeGraph(3), 1000);\r\n      expect(waves.length).toBe(1);\r\n      expect(waves[0].taskNodeIds.length).toBe(3);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('ResourceAwareWaveScheduler.plan() returns WavePlan[] with status=\"planned\" and the configured maxWorkers', () => {\r\n      const scheduler = new ResourceAwareWaveScheduler(makeGraph(3), { maxWorkers: 2 });\r\n      const waves: WavePlan[] = scheduler.plan();\r\n      expect(Array.isArray(waves)).toBe(true);\r\n      expect(waves.length).toBe(2);\r\n      expect(waves.every((w) => w.status === 'planned')).toBe(true);\r\n      expect(waves.every((w) => w.maxWorkers === 2)).toBe(true);\r\n    });\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  // 2. 边界条件 (5 tests)\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  describe('边界条件', () => {\r\n    it('maxWorkers=0 falls back to 1 (one task per wave, no throw)', () => {\r\n      // workerCap = Math.max(1, Math.floor(0)) === 1.\r\n      const waves = buildExecutionWaves(makeGraph(3), 0);\r\n      expect(waves.length).toBe(3);\r\n      for (const wave of waves) {\r\n        expect(wave.taskNodeIds.length).toBe(1);\r\n      }\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('maxWorkers=1 places exactly one task per wave', () => {\r\n      const waves = buildExecutionWaves(makeGraph(3), 1);\r\n      expect(waves.length).toBe(3);\r\n      expect(waves[0].taskNodeIds).toEqual(['task-1']);\r\n      expect(waves[1].taskNodeIds).toEqual(['task-2']);\r\n      expect(waves[2].taskNodeIds).toEqual(['task-3']);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('maxWorkers=1000 puts all tasks into a single wave', () => {\r\n      const waves = buildExecutionWaves(makeGraph(4), 1000);\r\n      expect(waves.length).toBe(1);\r\n      expect(waves[0].taskNodeIds.length).toBe(4);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('an orphan node (no deps, not depended on) is ready in the first wave', () => {\r\n      const graph: OrchestrationTaskGraph = {\r\n        graphRunId: 'run-o',\r\n        mode: 'router' as never,\r\n        status: 'planned',\r\n        nodes: [\r\n          makeNode('a', [], 'worker'),\r\n          makeNode('b', ['a'], 'worker'), // depends on a\r\n          makeNode('orphan', [], 'worker'), // no deps, not depended on\r\n        ],\r\n        edges: [],\r\n      };\r\n      const waves = buildExecutionWaves(graph, 10);\r\n      expect(waves[0].taskNodeIds).toContain('orphan');\r\n      expect(waves[0].taskNodeIds).toContain('a');\r\n      // b depends on a -> not ready in wave 1.\r\n      expect(waves[0].taskNodeIds).not.toContain('b');\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('ResourceAwareWaveScheduler with empty nodes produces an empty wave plan', () => {\r\n      const empty: OrchestrationTaskGraph = {\r\n        graphRunId: 'run-e',\r\n        mode: 'router' as never,\r\n        status: 'planned',\r\n        nodes: [],\r\n        edges: [],\r\n      };\r\n      const scheduler = new ResourceAwareWaveScheduler(empty, { maxWorkers: 4 });\r\n      expect(scheduler.plan()).toEqual([]);\r\n      expect(scheduler.getWaves()).toEqual([]);\r\n    });\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  // 3. 错误路径 (3 tests)\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  describe('错误路径', () => {\r\n    it('a cyclic graph causes buildExecutionWaves to terminate (no ready nodes -> empty result)', () => {\r\n      const cyclic: OrchestrationTaskGraph = {\r\n        graphRunId: 'run-c',\r\n        mode: 'router' as never,\r\n        status: 'planned',\r\n        nodes: [makeNode('a', ['b']), makeNode('b', ['a'])],\r\n        edges: [],\r\n      };\r\n      // Neither a nor b can ever become ready -> the while loop breaks with [].\r\n      const waves = buildExecutionWaves(cyclic);\r\n      expect(waves).toEqual([]);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('startWave on an unknown wave throws', () => {\r\n      const scheduler = new ResourceAwareWaveScheduler(makeGraph(3), { maxWorkers: 2 });\r\n      scheduler.plan();\r\n      expect(() => scheduler.startWave(99)).toThrow();\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('rePlan on a non-existent wave returns wave_not_found', () => {\r\n      const scheduler = new ResourceAwareWaveScheduler(makeGraph(3), { maxWorkers: 2 });\r\n      scheduler.plan();\r\n      const result = scheduler.rePlan({ appliesToWave: 99, maxWorkers: 4 });\r\n      expect(result.accepted).toBe(false);\r\n      if (!result.accepted) {\r\n        expect(result.reason).toBe('wave_not_found');\r\n        expect(result.waveNumber).toBe(99);\r\n      }\r\n    });\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  // 4. 属性测试 (3 tests)\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  describe('属性测试', () => {\r\n    it('buildExecutionWaves is deterministic (same input -> same output across 5 runs)', () => {\r\n      const graph = makeGraph(6);\r\n      const first = buildExecutionWaves(graph, 2);\r\n      for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {\r\n        expect(buildExecutionWaves(graph, 2)).toEqual(first);\r\n      }\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('topological order: a dependency is always scheduled in an earlier wave than its dependent', () => {\r\n      // task-2 depends on task-1; task-3 depends on task-2.\r\n      const graph = makeGraph(3, (_i, id) => {\r\n        if (id === 'task-2') return ['task-1'];\r\n        if (id === 'task-3') return ['task-2'];\r\n        return [];\r\n      });\r\n      const waves = buildExecutionWaves(graph, 10);\r\n      const waveOf = new Map<string, number>();\r\n      for (const w of waves) {\r\n        for (const id of w.taskNodeIds) waveOf.set(id, w.wave);\r\n      }\r\n      expect(waveOf.get('task-1')!).toBeLessThan(waveOf.get('task-2')!);\r\n      expect(waveOf.get('task-2')!).toBeLessThan(waveOf.get('task-3')!);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('wave count never exceeds ceil(tasks / maxWorkers) for independent tasks', () => {\r\n      const cases: Array<{ tasks: number; workers: number }> = [\r\n        { tasks: 5, workers: 2 },\r\n        { tasks: 7, workers: 3 },\r\n        { tasks: 10, workers: 4 },\r\n      ];\r\n      for (const { tasks, workers } of cases) {\r\n        const waves = buildExecutionWaves(makeGraph(tasks), workers);\r\n        const expected = Math.ceil(tasks / workers);\r\n        expect(waves.length).toBeLessThanOrEqual(expected);\r\n      }\r\n    });\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  // 5. 并发测试 (2 tests)\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  describe('并发测试', () => {\r\n    it('two independent scheduler instances do not interfere with each other', () => {\r\n      const s1 = new ResourceAwareWaveScheduler(makeGraph(3), { maxWorkers: 2 });\r\n      const s2 = new ResourceAwareWaveScheduler(makeGraph(5), { maxWorkers: 1 });\r\n      const w1 = s1.plan();\r\n      const w2 = s2.plan();\r\n      expect(w1.length).toBe(2);\r\n      expect(w2.length).toBe(5);\r\n      // Mutating s1's wave state must not affect s2.\r\n      s1.startWave(1);\r\n      expect(s2.getWaveStatus(1)).toBe('planned');\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('consecutive plan() calls are idempotent (later plan overwrites the former)', () => {\r\n      const scheduler = new ResourceAwareWaveScheduler(makeGraph(4), { maxWorkers: 2 });\r\n      const first = scheduler.plan();\r\n      const second = scheduler.plan();\r\n      expect(second.length).toBe(first.length);\r\n      expect(second.map((w) => w.wave)).toEqual(first.map((w) => w.wave));\r\n      expect(second.every((w) => w.status === 'planned')).toBe(true);\r\n    });\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  // 6. 压力测试 (2 tests)\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  describe('压力测试', () => {\r\n    it('100 task nodes + 10 workers build waves in under 100ms', () => {\r\n      const graph = makeGraph(100);\r\n      const start = Date.now();\r\n      const waves = buildExecutionWaves(graph, 10);\r\n      const elapsed = Date.now() - start;\r\n      expect(waves.length).toBe(10); // 100 / 10\r\n      expect(elapsed).toBeLessThan(100);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('500 nodes + 50 workers do not crash the planner', () => {\r\n      const graph = makeGraph(500);\r\n      const waves = buildExecutionWaves(graph, 50);\r\n      expect(waves).toBeDefined();\r\n      expect(waves.length).toBe(10); // 500 / 50\r\n      // Every node scheduled exactly once.\r\n      const totalScheduled = waves.reduce((sum, w) => sum + w.taskNodeIds.length, 0);\r\n      expect(totalScheduled).toBe(500);\r\n    });\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  // 7. 集成测试 (3 tests)\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  describe('集成测试', () => {\r\n    it('startWave -> completeWave -> rePlan lifecycle: completed wave rejected, planned wave accepted', () => {\r\n      const scheduler = new ResourceAwareWaveScheduler(makeGraph(4), { maxWorkers: 2 });\r\n      const waves = scheduler.plan();\r\n      expect(waves.length).toBe(2);\r\n      scheduler.startWave(1);\r\n      scheduler.completeWave(1);\r\n      // Re-planning the completed wave 1 is rejected (wave immutability).\r\n      const rejected = scheduler.rePlan({ appliesToWave: 1, maxWorkers: 3 });\r\n      expect(rejected.accepted).toBe(false);\r\n      if (!rejected.accepted) {\r\n        expect(rejected.reason).toBe('wave_started');\r\n      }\r\n      // Re-planning the still-planned wave 2 with a new worker cap is accepted.\r\n      const accepted = scheduler.rePlan({ appliesToWave: 2, maxWorkers: 3 });\r\n      expect(accepted.accepted).toBe(true);\r\n      if (accepted.accepted) {\r\n        expect(accepted.replannedWaves).toContain(2);\r\n      }\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('rePlan on an already-completed wave returns reason wave_started', () => {\r\n      const scheduler = new ResourceAwareWaveScheduler(makeGraph(2), { maxWorkers: 1 });\r\n      scheduler.plan();\r\n      scheduler.startWave(1);\r\n      scheduler.completeWave(1);\r\n      const result = scheduler.rePlan({ appliesToWave: 1, maxWorkers: 5 });\r\n      expect(result.accepted).toBe(false);\r\n      if (!result.accepted) {\r\n        expect(result.reason).toBe('wave_started');\r\n        expect(result.waveNumber).toBe(1);\r\n      }\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('getWaves returns waves sorted by wave number ascending', () => {\r\n      const scheduler = new ResourceAwareWaveScheduler(makeGraph(5), { maxWorkers: 2 });\r\n      scheduler.plan();\r\n      const waves = scheduler.getWaves();\r\n      const numbers = waves.map((w) => w.wave);\r\n      const sorted = [...numbers].sort((a, b) => a - b);\r\n      expect(numbers).toEqual(sorted);\r\n      // Expected wave numbers are 1..3 (5 tasks / 2 workers).\r\n      expect(numbers).toEqual([1, 2, 3]);\r\n    });\r\n  });\r\n});\r\n=====A3=====\r\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\r\n\r\nimport {\r\n  type AnomalyClassifierInput,\r\n  type AnomalyPatternKind,\r\n  classifyAnomalyPattern,\r\n  resolveAnomalyPatternForReviewer,\r\n} from '../../../openclaw_runtime/src/agents/anomaly-classifier.js';\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * A3 deep tests — Runtime Resilience anomaly classifier.\r\n *\r\n * Covers:\r\n * - agents/anomaly-classifier.ts (classifyAnomalyPattern, resolveAnomalyPatternForReviewer,\r\n *   AnomalyPatternKind, AnomalyPattern, AnomalyClassifierInput)\r\n *\r\n * Note on import depth: tests live in tests/unit/deep/, so the relative path to\r\n * the runtime tree is ../../../openclaw_runtime/src/... (three levels up to root).\r\n *\r\n * Note on thresholds: the threshold constants (TOOL_FAILURE_BURST_THRESHOLD, etc.)\r\n * are module-private in anomaly-classifier.ts (not exported). The local constants\r\n * below mirror the documented design values and are used only to make boundary\r\n * assertions self-documenting.\r\n */\r\n\r\n// Mirrors anomaly-classifier.ts thresholds (not exported; values per design spec).\r\nconst TOOL_FAILURE_BURST_THRESHOLD = 3;\r\nconst NO_PROGRESS_TICK_THRESHOLD = 2;\r\nconst TOKEN_BLOWUP_RATIO = 1.5;\r\nconst REPAIR_STORM_RATIO = 0.6;\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * Build a feature-flags object for resolveAnomalyPatternForReviewer without\r\n * importing the full RuntimeFeatureConfig type (only the resilience.anomalyClassifierPilot\r\n * field is read). Cast to any to avoid coupling the test to the wide config shape.\r\n */\r\nfunction featureFlags(mode: 'shadow' | 'off'): unknown {\r\n  return { resilience: { anomalyClassifierPilot: mode } };\r\n}\r\n\r\ndescribe('A3 deep — anomaly-classifier', () => {\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  // 1. 功能完整性 (8 tests)\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  describe('功能完整性', () => {\r\n    it('tool_failure_burst triggers when recentToolFailureCount >= threshold', () => {\r\n      const result = classifyAnomalyPattern({\r\n        tick: 1,\r\n        repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n        maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n        maxTicks: 10,\r\n        recentToolFailureCount: TOOL_FAILURE_BURST_THRESHOLD,\r\n      });\r\n      expect(result).not.toBeNull();\r\n      expect(result!.kind).toBe('tool_failure_burst');\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('no_progress triggers when tick past halfway with no failures and no progress', () => {\r\n      const result = classifyAnomalyPattern({\r\n        tick: 5,\r\n        repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n        maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n        maxTicks: 10,\r\n        failures: [],\r\n      });\r\n      expect(result).not.toBeNull();\r\n      expect(result!.kind).toBe('no_progress');\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('token_blowup triggers when tokenUsage / tokenBudget >= blowup ratio', () => {\r\n      const result = classifyAnomalyPattern({\r\n        tick: 1,\r\n        repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n        maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n        maxTicks: 10,\r\n        tokenUsage: { input: 0, output: 0, total: 2000 },\r\n        tokenBudget: 1000,\r\n      });\r\n      expect(result).not.toBeNull();\r\n      expect(result!.kind).toBe('token_blowup');\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('repair_storm triggers when repairTicksUsed / maxRepairTicks >= storm ratio', () => {\r\n      const result = classifyAnomalyPattern({\r\n        tick: 1,\r\n        repairTicksUsed: 7,\r\n        maxRepairTicks: 10,\r\n        maxTicks: 10,\r\n      });\r\n      expect(result).not.toBeNull();\r\n      expect(result!.kind).toBe('repair_storm');\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('stuck_loop triggers when noProgressHash is unchanged from the previous tick', () => {\r\n      const result = classifyAnomalyPattern({\r\n        tick: 1,\r\n        repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n        maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n        maxTicks: 10,\r\n        noProgressHash: 'abc',\r\n        previousNoProgressHash: 'abc',\r\n      });\r\n      expect(result).not.toBeNull();\r\n      expect(result!.kind).toBe('stuck_loop');\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('classifyAnomalyPattern returns null when no anomaly is detected', () => {\r\n      const result = classifyAnomalyPattern({\r\n        tick: 1,\r\n        repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n        maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n        maxTicks: 10,\r\n        failures: [],\r\n        recentToolFailureCount: 0,\r\n      });\r\n      expect(result).toBeNull();\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it(\"resolveAnomalyPatternForReviewer with flag='shadow' returns the classified pattern\", () => {\r\n      const input: AnomalyClassifierInput = {\r\n        tick: 1,\r\n        repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n        maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n        maxTicks: 10,\r\n        recentToolFailureCount: 5,\r\n      };\r\n      const result = resolveAnomalyPatternForReviewer(\r\n        featureFlags('shadow') as never,\r\n        input,\r\n      );\r\n      expect(result).not.toBeUndefined();\r\n      expect(result).not.toBeNull();\r\n      expect(result!.kind).toBe('tool_failure_burst');\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it(\"resolveAnomalyPatternForReviewer with flag='off' returns undefined (flag-off parity)\", () => {\r\n      const input: AnomalyClassifierInput = {\r\n        tick: 1,\r\n        repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n        maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n        maxTicks: 10,\r\n        recentToolFailureCount: 5,\r\n      };\r\n      const result = resolveAnomalyPatternForReviewer(\r\n        featureFlags('off') as never,\r\n        input,\r\n      );\r\n      expect(result).toBeUndefined();\r\n    });\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  // 2. 边界条件 (6 tests)\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  describe('边界条件', () => {\r\n    it('tick=0 produces no anomaly (no_progress requires tick >= NO_PROGRESS_TICK_THRESHOLD)', () => {\r\n      // 0 is strictly below NO_PROGRESS_TICK_THRESHOLD, so no_progress cannot fire.\r\n      expect(0).toBeLessThan(NO_PROGRESS_TICK_THRESHOLD);\r\n      const result = classifyAnomalyPattern({\r\n        tick: 0,\r\n        repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n        maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n        maxTicks: 10,\r\n      });\r\n      expect(result).toBeNull();\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('maxTicks=0 is safe from division-by-zero (no crash, no false positive)', () => {\r\n      const result = classifyAnomalyPattern({\r\n        tick: 0,\r\n        repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n        maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n        maxTicks: 0,\r\n      });\r\n      expect(result).toBeNull();\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('maxRepairTicks=0 disables repair_storm (guard prevents division by zero)', () => {\r\n      // repairTicksUsed is high but maxRepairTicks=0 -> the guard skips the check.\r\n      const result = classifyAnomalyPattern({\r\n        tick: 1,\r\n        repairTicksUsed: 5,\r\n        maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n        maxTicks: 10,\r\n      });\r\n      expect(result).toBeNull();\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('tokenBudget=0 disables token_blowup (guard prevents division by zero)', () => {\r\n      const result = classifyAnomalyPattern({\r\n        tick: 1,\r\n        repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n        maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n        maxTicks: 10,\r\n        tokenUsage: { input: 0, output: 0, total: 9999 },\r\n        tokenBudget: 0,\r\n      });\r\n      expect(result).toBeNull();\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('failures=undefined and recentToolFailureCount=undefined yields no tool_failure_burst (defaults to 0)', () => {\r\n      const result = classifyAnomalyPattern({\r\n        tick: 1,\r\n        repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n        maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n        maxTicks: 10,\r\n      });\r\n      expect(result).toBeNull();\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('exactly-at-threshold values trigger (boundaries are inclusive >=)', () => {\r\n      // tool_failure_burst at exactly 3 failures.\r\n      const t1 = classifyAnomalyPattern({\r\n        tick: 1,\r\n        repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n        maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n        maxTicks: 10,\r\n        recentToolFailureCount: TOOL_FAILURE_BURST_THRESHOLD,\r\n      });\r\n      expect(t1!.kind).toBe('tool_failure_burst');\r\n\r\n      // repair_storm at exactly the storm ratio (10 * REPAIR_STORM_RATIO = 6).\r\n      const t2 = classifyAnomalyPattern({\r\n        tick: 1,\r\n        repairTicksUsed: 10 * REPAIR_STORM_RATIO,\r\n        maxRepairTicks: 10,\r\n        maxTicks: 10,\r\n      });\r\n      expect(t2!.kind).toBe('repair_storm');\r\n\r\n      // token_blowup at exactly the blowup ratio (1000 * TOKEN_BLOWUP_RATIO = 1500).\r\n      const t3 = classifyAnomalyPattern({\r\n        tick: 1,\r\n        repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n        maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n        maxTicks: 10,\r\n        tokenUsage: { input: 0, output: 0, total: 1000 * TOKEN_BLOWUP_RATIO },\r\n        tokenBudget: 1000,\r\n      });\r\n      expect(t3!.kind).toBe('token_blowup');\r\n    });\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  // 3. 错误路径 (3 tests)\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  describe('错误路径', () => {\r\n    it('resolveAnomalyPatternForReviewer degrades to undefined when featureFlags is undefined', () => {\r\n      const input: AnomalyClassifierInput = {\r\n        tick: 1,\r\n        repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n        maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n        maxTicks: 10,\r\n        recentToolFailureCount: 5,\r\n      };\r\n      const result = resolveAnomalyPatternForReviewer(undefined, input);\r\n      expect(result).toBeUndefined();\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('resolveAnomalyPatternForReviewer degrades to undefined when featureFlags is null', () => {\r\n      const input: AnomalyClassifierInput = {\r\n        tick: 1,\r\n        repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n        maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n        maxTicks: 10,\r\n        recentToolFailureCount: 5,\r\n      };\r\n      const result = resolveAnomalyPatternForReviewer(null as never, input);\r\n      expect(result).toBeUndefined();\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('input with only required fields present uses sensible defaults (no crash, no false positive)', () => {\r\n      // All optional anomaly-signal fields omitted; only tick/repair/maxRepair/maxTicks given.\r\n      const result = classifyAnomalyPattern({\r\n        tick: 0,\r\n        repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n        maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n        maxTicks: 0,\r\n      });\r\n      expect(result).toBeNull();\r\n    });\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  // 4. 属性测试 (2 tests)\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  describe('属性测试', () => {\r\n    it('classifyAnomalyPattern is deterministic (same input -> same output across 10 runs)', () => {\r\n      const input: AnomalyClassifierInput = {\r\n        tick: 3,\r\n        repairTicksUsed: 8,\r\n        maxRepairTicks: 10,\r\n        maxTicks: 10,\r\n        recentToolFailureCount: 4,\r\n      };\r\n      const first = classifyAnomalyPattern(input);\r\n      expect(first).not.toBeNull();\r\n      for (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) {\r\n        expect(classifyAnomalyPattern(input)).toEqual(first);\r\n      }\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('non-anomalous inputs always return null (across multiple variations)', () => {\r\n      const noAnomalyInputs: AnomalyClassifierInput[] = [\r\n        { tick: 0, repairTicksUsed: 0, maxRepairTicks: 0, maxTicks: 10 },\r\n        { tick: 1, repairTicksUsed: 0, maxRepairTicks: 0, maxTicks: 10, failures: [] },\r\n        { tick: 1, repairTicksUsed: 1, maxRepairTicks: 10, maxTicks: 10 }, // 0.1 < 0.6\r\n        {\r\n          tick: 1,\r\n          repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n          maxRepairTicks: 10,\r\n          maxTicks: 10,\r\n          tokenUsage: { input: 0, output: 0, total: 100 },\r\n          tokenBudget: 1000,\r\n        }, // 0.1 < 1.5\r\n      ];\r\n      for (const input of noAnomalyInputs) {\r\n        expect(classifyAnomalyPattern(input)).toBeNull();\r\n      }\r\n    });\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  // 5. 压力测试 (2 tests)\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  describe('压力测试', () => {\r\n    it('100 consecutive calls (simulating 100 Mission ticks) complete quickly', () => {\r\n      const start = Date.now();\r\n      for (let i = 0; i < 100; i++) {\r\n        classifyAnomalyPattern({\r\n          tick: i,\r\n          repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n          maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n          maxTicks: 100,\r\n        });\r\n      }\r\n      const elapsed = Date.now() - start;\r\n      // Pure function with no I/O -> should be well under 200ms for 100 calls.\r\n      expect(elapsed).toBeLessThan(200);\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('a failures array with 1000 elements does not crash (and still classifies)', () => {\r\n      const failures = Array.from({ length: 1000 }, (_, i) => `failure-${i}`);\r\n      const result = classifyAnomalyPattern({\r\n        tick: 1,\r\n        repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n        maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n        maxTicks: 10,\r\n        failures,\r\n      });\r\n      expect(result).not.toBeNull();\r\n      expect(result!.kind).toBe('tool_failure_burst');\r\n    });\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  // 6. 集成测试 (2 tests)\r\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  describe('集成测试', () => {\r\n    it('every detected pattern.kind is a member of the AnomalyPatternKind union', () => {\r\n      const validKinds: AnomalyPatternKind[] = [\r\n        'tool_failure_burst',\r\n        'no_progress',\r\n        'token_blowup',\r\n        'repair_storm',\r\n        'stuck_loop',\r\n      ];\r\n      const inputs: AnomalyClassifierInput[] = [\r\n        {\r\n          tick: 1,\r\n          repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n          maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n          maxTicks: 10,\r\n          recentToolFailureCount: 3,\r\n        }, // tool_failure_burst\r\n        { tick: 5, repairTicksUsed: 0, maxRepairTicks: 0, maxTicks: 10, failures: [] }, // no_progress\r\n        {\r\n          tick: 1,\r\n          repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n          maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n          maxTicks: 10,\r\n          tokenUsage: { input: 0, output: 0, total: 2000 },\r\n          tokenBudget: 1000,\r\n        }, // token_blowup\r\n        { tick: 1, repairTicksUsed: 7, maxRepairTicks: 10, maxTicks: 10 }, // repair_storm\r\n        {\r\n          tick: 1,\r\n          repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n          maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n          maxTicks: 10,\r\n          noProgressHash: 'x',\r\n          previousNoProgressHash: 'x',\r\n        }, // stuck_loop\r\n      ];\r\n      for (const input of inputs) {\r\n        const r = classifyAnomalyPattern(input);\r\n        expect(r).not.toBeNull();\r\n        expect(validKinds).toContain(r!.kind);\r\n      }\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    it('every detected pattern has a valid severity value (low | medium | high)', () => {\r\n      const result = classifyAnomalyPattern({\r\n        tick: 1,\r\n        repairTicksUsed: 0,\r\n        maxRepairTicks: 0,\r\n        maxTicks: 10,\r\n        recentToolFailureCount: 5,\r\n      });\r\n      expect(result).not.toBeNull();\r\n      expect(['low', 'medium', 'high']).toContain(result!.severity);\r\n    });\r\n  });\r\n});\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_97","type":"reasoning","text":"So there is a \"deep\" test structure. The task wants me to:\n1. Add a4-deep test (test file `tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts` per targetScope)\n2. Fix spec drift in a4-decision-quality-pilot.md requiredTests\n3. Create harness-gap-a04-decision-quality-pilot-reverify.md\n4. Create docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a04-decision-quality-gate.md\n5. Create docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a04-acceptance.json\n6. Create docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/A04-SHA256SUMS\n\nWait — targetScope lists:\n- harness/specs/tasks/a4-decision-quality-pilot.md\n- tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts\n- harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a04-decision-quality-pilot-reverify.md\n- docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a04-decision-quality-gate.md\n- docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a04-acceptance.json\n- docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/A04-SHA256SUMS\n\nThe acceptance criteria mention:\n- 判据1: decision-quality-auditor, deprecation-counters, a4-deep 有当前断言 → PASS\n- 判据4: trace-truncation 断言 a4→a3→a5 先于 a1 被丢弃 → we found `observability-namespace.test.ts` assertions with spanDropPriority.\n- 修正 spec drift: requiredTests 补入 auditor、a4-deep 与 degradation-order 测试, 并加 A04 coverage 守卫.\n\nSo the requiredTests need to include:\n- decision-quality-auditor test — but there's no test file for decision-quality-auditor! I need to create one, or reference the deep test. Hmm. Let me check `tests/unit/deep/` — only a1,a2,a3 deep. The acceptance criteria says \"decision-quality-auditor、deprecation-counters 与 a4-deep 有当前断言\". So maybe I need to create a4-deep.test.ts too? But targetScope doesn't list it... Actually targetScope lists `tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts`. But the criteria says the requiredTests should be \"补入 auditor、a4-deep 与 degradation-order 测试\". So the spec's requiredTests should include a file for auditor, a4-deep, and degradation-order.\n\nLet me look at how a1/a2/a3 specs' requiredTests reference deep tests. Let me check a1 