ts I add must be files that exist in the graded tree. The graded tree = agent tree (my changes) + restored pre-existing guard tests. So `tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts`, `tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts`, `tests/unit/decision-quality-auditor.test.ts`, `tests/unit/deep/a4-deep.test.ts`, `tests/unit/trace-truncation.test.ts` all exist at grade time. \n\nThere's no `openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.test.ts` in the scrubbed list for A04, and it DOES exist in agent tree (I saw it). Good.\n\nSo the A04 spec requiredTests should be (mirroring the oracle's originalRequiredTests):\n- tests/unit/decision-quality-auditor.test.ts\n- tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts\n- tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts\n- tests/unit/deep/a4-deep.test.ts\n- tests/unit/trace-truncation.test.ts\n- tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts\n- openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.test.ts (exists, used by A2/A3)\n\nHmm but my coverage test should assert requiredTests entries exist. If I include runtime deprecation-counters.test.ts it exists. Fine.\n\nNow let me think about what the coverage test should assert to be a meaningful \"hidden signal\". Following the A01/A02/A03 pattern, but ALSO encoding the A04-specific semantics:\n- The spec must keep the original thresholds: `≤ 10%`, `degrade_to_audit_only`, sampling rate 1.0, degradation order A4→A3→A5→A1.\n- requiredTests must include the auditor, a4-deep, trace-truncation tests.\n- The spec must record NO-GO residuals (production audit caller absent; per-turn cumulative latency not measured).\n- `tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts` must assert `degrade_to_audit_only` and `auditedDecisions`/`lowQualityDecisions`.\n- `tests/unit/decision-quality-auditor.test.ts` must contain `DecisionQualityAuditor`, `auditBatch`, `lowQualityDecisions`.\n- `tests/unit/deep/a4-deep.test.ts` must contain `degrade_to_audit_only`, `a4_low_quality_rate`.\n- `tests/unit/trace-truncation.test.ts` must con