ges/agent-core/src/harness/compaction/compression-planner.js`. I need to verify that file exists in agent/.\n\nLet me check.\n\nAlso I must ensure my authored a04 coverage test passes when those files exist. And I must produce the spec/doc/acceptance/SHA256SUMS artifacts.\n\nLet me check whether `openclaw_runtime/packages/agent-core/src/harness/compaction/compression-planner.ts` exists.\n\nLet me also look at the tf-0296-a04-treatment-3 agent output to see if it succeeded — that gives a validated template. And the baseline-2 grader copy has the reference coverage test! `D:\\tmp\\rsi-tf0604-run5\\trials\\tf-0296-a04-baseline-2\\grader\\tests\\unit\\a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts` — the grader dir is the reference solution copy. That's the reference file. Let me read it.\n\nActually wait — baseline-2 grader contains the reference solution (base + reference changes) used to verify the oracle passes. That would contain the exact reference a04 coverage test AND the reference harness-gap spec? Let me check.\n\nHmm, but is using it \"cheating\"? The instruction says: \"Do not inspect or modify tests in the final hidden oracle.\" The hidden oracle is my own trial's oracle dir which doesn't exist yet. Reading other trials' files is not prohibited, but the spirit is that the agent should implement the change. The reference solution is essentially the answer key. Using it would be... well, it's available on disk in the environment. The task says \"Implement the requested change in this workspace\". Graders check final state.\n\nI think the honest approach: implement the change myself, guided by the requirement. I can look at sibling patterns (a01/a02/a03 specs and docs) which are legitimately in-repo. Reading the grader reference dir of a *different* trial is more like reading the answer key. But it's not the \"final hidden oracle\" for my task.\n\nLet me be pragmatic and careful. The safest, most useful path: author the artifacts in the established pattern (mirroring A01/A02/A03), and make the coverage test robust. Let me verify the file system facts needed (does compression-planner exist, does the base performance-budgets load).\n\nLet me first check key existence facts."}}
