est.ts (must be authored!)\n\nAnd it checks:\n- spec contains `- <each path>` for all 7\n- existsSync each path\n- deprecation-counters.ts contains `action: \"degrade_to_audit_only\"`\n- trace-recorder.ts contains \"a4 > a3 > a5 > a2 > a1 > a6 > core\"\n- trace-truncation.test.ts contains \"drops lowest-priority spans first\" and \"a4, a3, a5 should be dropped\"\n- development-manual.md contains \"A4 — Decision Quality (offline pure functions only)\" and \"A4 is called ONLY via explicit dev-tool invocation\"\n- no file under openclaw_runtime/src (other than decision-quality-auditor) contains \"DecisionQualityAuditor\" — wait, this is the `.filter(file => !file.includes(\"decision-quality-auditor\"))` — so the only offender check. Currently decision-quality-auditor.ts is in openclaw_runtime/src, so it's excluded; no other file references it. Good.\n- existsSync(scripts/a4-decision-quality-audit.mts)\n- package.json scripts[\"a4:decision-quality-audit\"] contains \"a4-decision-quality-audit.mts\"\n\nHmm wait. But that's the *grader* copy in baseline-2. That's not necessarily what will be applied to MY trial. My trial's hiddenSignalPaths = [\"tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts\"] — meaning MY hidden test is the a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts that *I* author! Let me re-read.\n\nFrom manifest: `hiddenSignalPaths: [\"tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts\"]` and `preexistingGuardPaths: [decision-quality-auditor.test.ts, deprecation-counters.test.ts, performance-budgets.test.ts, deep/a4-deep.test.ts, trace-truncation.test.ts]`.\n\nHmm, so `a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts` is a \"hidden signal path\" — meaning it's MY authored artifact which is the signal? But it's hidden... Actually for A01/A02/A03, the coverage test was also in hiddenSignalPaths, and the diff showed the agent-authored file was NOT in the diff (diff.added was empty!) — because in those trials the agent produced nothing (timed out / failed) OR because the coverage test is scrubbed?\n\nWait. Look at tf-029